BT /F2 13 Tf 35 755 Td (Complete Cotton \(Gossypium spp.\) Agronomy, IPM & Production Manual - Page 1) Tj ET

BT /F2 10 Tf 35 732 Td (1. Taxonomy & Cultivated Species) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 719 Td (- Gossypium hirsutum \(Upland/American Cotton\): Tetraploid \(2n=52\); accounts for >90% of global commercial production.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 707 Td (- Gossypium barbadense \(Egyptian/Pima/Sea Island\): Tetraploid \(2n=52\); prized for extra-long staple \(ELS\) luxury fibers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 695 Td (- Gossypium arboreum \(Tree Cotton\) & G. herbaceum \(Levant Cotton\): Diploids \(2n=26\); drought & pest tolerant short-staple.) Tj ET

BT /F2 10 Tf 35 675 Td (2. Edaphic \(Soil\) & Climatic Requirements) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 662 Td (- Soil Type: Deep, friable, well-drained black cotton soils \(Vertisols\), alluvial, or red loamy soils with good moisture retention.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 650 Td (- Soil pH & Salinity: Optimal pH 6.0 to 8.0; moderately tolerant to salinity \(EC threshold ~7.7 dS/m\), highly sensitive to waterlogging.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 638 Td (- Climate: Requires 180-200 frost-free days, abundant sunshine. Germination: >16 C; Vegetative: 21-27 C; Fruiting: 27-32 C day / cool nights.) Tj ET

BT /F2 10 Tf 35 618 Td (3. Crop Phenology & Growth Stages \(Days After Sowing - DAS\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 605 Td (- Emergence to Seedling \(0-30 DAS\): Epigeal germination in 5-10 days; deep taproot establishment; high vulnerability to thrips/aphids.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 593 Td (- Squaring \(35-55 DAS\): Appearance of floral buds \(squares\); rapid nodal development and canopy expansion.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 581 Td (- Peak Flowering to Boll Formation \(60-100 DAS\): White flowers turn pink then shed petals; peak water and potassium demand.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 569 Td (- Boll Maturation & Dehiscence \(110-160+ DAS\): Fiber elongation \(days 1-20 post-anthesis\) and secondary wall thickening \(days 20-45\).) Tj ET

BT /F2 10 Tf 35 549 Td (4. Land Preparation, Seed Treatment & Sowing Agronomy) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 536 Td (- Tillage: Deep summer plowing \(20-30 cm\) with moldboard plow every 2-3 years to expose pupae and perennial weeds \(Cyperus rotundus\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 524 Td (- Acid Delinting: Treat fuzzy seed with concentrated H2SO4 \(100 ml/kg seed\) for 2-3 mins, wash thoroughly, and lime-neutralize.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 512 Td (- Seed Dressing \(per kg\): Imidacloprid 70 WS \(5-7 g\) for sucking pests + Carboxin 75 WP \(2 g\) + Trichoderma viride \(10 g\) for root rot.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 500 Td (- Seed Rate & Spacing: Bt Hybrids: 1.5-2.5 kg/ha at 90-120 x 45-60 cm. HDPS \(High Density Planting System\): 10-12 kg/ha at 60 x 10 cm.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 488 Td (- Refugia Mandate: Plant 5% non-Bt cotton \(or 20% in bag-in-bag systems\) to delay bollworm resistance to Cry1Ac and Cry2Ab toxins.) Tj ET

BT /F2 10 Tf 35 468 Td (5. Integrated Nutrient Management \(INM\) & Physiological Disorders) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 455 Td (- Organic Manuring: Incorporate 10-12 tonnes/ha of well-decomposed Farm Yard Manure \(FYM\) or vermicompost 2-3 weeks prior to sowing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 443 Td (- NPK Dosage: Hybrids: 120-150:60:60 kg N:P2O5:K2O/ha. Varieties: 60-90:30:30 kg/ha. Apply 100% P & K + 25% N as basal dose.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 431 Td (- Top Dressing: Apply remaining 75% Nitrogen in 3 equal splits at 30 DAS \(thinning\), 60 DAS \(squaring\), and 90 DAS \(peak flowering\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 419 Td (- Micronutrients: Soil apply ZnSO4 \(25 kg/ha\) and Borax \(5-10 kg/ha\) in deficient soils; Boron prevents hollow-heart and square shedding.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 407 Td (- Foliar Nutrition: Spray 2% KNO3 \(13:0:45\) or 2% DAP at 60, 75, and 90 DAS to boost boll weight and fiber micronaire.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 395 Td (- Leaf Reddening \(Lalya\): Caused by Mg deficiency and night temperature drops. Manage with 1% MgSO4 + 1% Urea foliar spray at 60-75 DAS.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 383 Td (- Tirak \(Bad Boll Opening\): Premature cracking with immature lint on saline/light soils. Mitigate via timely irrigation and K application.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 371 Td (- Physiological Square Shedding: Spray Naphthalene Acetic Acid \(NAA / Planofix\) at 10-20 ppm at flower initiation and 15 days later.) Tj ET

BT /F2 10 Tf 35 351 Td (6. Irrigation Scheduling, Weed Control & Canopy Management) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 338 Td (- Water Requirement: 700-1200 mm total. Critical moisture stages: Squaring \(35-45 DAS\), Flowering \(60-75 DAS\), Boll Development \(85-105 DAS\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 326 Td (- Irrigation Methods: Furrow irrigation \(alternate furrow saves 30% water\) or Drip Fertigation \(increases water-use efficiency by 40-50%\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 314 Td (- Pre-Emergence Weed Control: Spray Pendimethalin 30 EC \(3.3 L/ha\) or Pendimethalin 38.7 CS \(1.75 L/ha\) within 48 hours of sowing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 302 Td (- Post-Emergence & Intercultivation: Hoeing at 25 and 45 DAS; directed spray of Pyrithiobac-sodium 10 EC \(625 ml/ha\) + Quizalofop-ethyl.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 290 Td (- Canopy Regulation: Detopping terminal bud at 90-100 DAS or spraying Mepiquat Chloride 5% AS \(50 ppm / 1 ml/L\) at 60 and 75 DAS.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
