BT /F2 13 Tf 35 755 Td (Complete Cotton \(Gossypium spp.\) Agronomy, IPM & Production Manual - Page 2) Tj ET

BT /F2 10 Tf 35 732 Td (7. Comprehensive Integrated Pest Management \(IPM\) & Economic Threshold Levels \(ETL\)) Tj ET

BT /F2 9 Tf 35 716 Td (A. Bollworm Complex \(Lepidoptera\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 704 Td (- American Bollworm \(Helicoverpa armigera\): Larvae feed on squares/bolls with half body outside; circular bore holes with flared bracts.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 692 Td (  ETL: 1 larva/plant or 5-10% damaged fruiting bodies. Control: HaNPV \(250-500 LE/ha\), Emamectin benzoate 5 SG \(0.4 g/L\), Chlorantraniliprole.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 680 Td (- Pink Bollworm \(Pectinophora gossypiella\): Internal feeder; causes 'rosette flowers', interlocular burrowing, stained lint, ruined seeds.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 668 Td (  ETL: 10% rosette flowers or 8 moths/pheromone trap/night for 3 nights. Control: Gossyplure traps \(20/ha\), Profenofos 50 EC or Spinetoram.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 656 Td (- Spotted Bollworm \(Earias vittella & E. insulana\): Terminal shoot boring \(drooping/withering\) in early stages; lint-fouling frass in bolls.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 644 Td (  ETL: 5% withered shoots or damaged bolls. Control: Clip and destroy infested shoots; release Trichogramma chilonis \(1.5 lakh/ha\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 632 Td (- Tobacco Caterpillar \(Spodoptera litura\): Gregarious larvae skeletonize leaves. Control: Castor trap crop; SlNPV; Novaluron 10 EC.) Tj ET

BT /F2 9 Tf 35 614 Td (B. Sap-Sucking & Foliage Pest Complex) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 602 Td (- Whitefly \(Bemisia tabaci\): Sucks phloem sap, excretes honeydew \(sooty mold\), transmits CLCuD. ETL: 6-8 adults or 20 nymphs/leaf.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 590 Td (  Control: Yellow sticky traps \(25/ha\); Neem oil 0.5%; Diafenthiuron 50 WP \(1.2 g/L\), Pyriproxyfen 10 EC \(2 ml/L\), or Spiromesifen.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 578 Td (- Leafhopper / Jassids \(Amrasca biguttula biguttula\): Causes downward leaf curling, yellowing, marginal reddening, and 'hopper burn'.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 566 Td (  ETL: 2-3 nymphs/leaf or Grade II injury. Control: Grow hairy varieties; spray Flonicamid 50 WG \(0.3 g/L\) or Dinotefuran 20 SG \(0.3 g/L\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 554 Td (- Aphids \(Aphis gossypii\) & Thrips \(Thrips tabaci\): Aphids cause crinkling; Thrips lacerate leaves causing silvery patches and brittle curl.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 542 Td (  ETL: 10-15% infested plants \(Aphids\) or 10 thrips/leaf. Control: Conserve Coccinellids/Chrysoperla; spray Thiamethoxam or Spinosad.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 530 Td (- Mealybug \(Phenacoccus solenopsis\): Waxy colonies on stems cause stunted, bushy shoots. Control: Destroy Parthenium weeds; Buprofezin 25 SC.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 518 Td (- Red & Dusky Cotton Bugs \(Dysdercus koenigii & Oxycarenus laetus\): Stain lint yellow/red and reduce seed oil content and viability.) Tj ET

BT /F2 10 Tf 35 498 Td (8. Plant Pathology & Disease Management) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 485 Td (- Cotton Leaf Curl Disease \(CLCuD\): Begomovirus \(Geminiviridae\) vectored by Bemisia tabaci. Symptoms: Vein thickening, cup-shaped enations.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 473 Td (  Management: Eradicate weed hosts \(Sida, Abutilon\); sow tolerant hybrids; strictly avoid synthetic pyrethroids to prevent whitefly resurgence.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 461 Td (- Bacterial Blight / Blackarm \(Xanthomonas citri pv. malvacearum\): Water-soaked angular leaf spots, vein blight, black stem lesions, boll rot.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 449 Td (  Management: Acid delinting; spray Copper Oxychloride 50 WP \(2.5 g/L\) + Streptocycline \(100 ppm\) at 15-day intervals on symptom appearance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 437 Td (- Fusarium Wilt \(F. oxysporum f. sp. vasinfectum\) & Verticillium Wilt \(V. dahliae\): Yellowing, wilting, dark brown vascular ring discoloration.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 425 Td (  Management: Potash application; seed & soil application of Trichoderma harzianum + Pseudomonas fluorescens; spot drench Carbendazim \(1 g/L\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 413 Td (- Root Rot \(Rhizoctonia bataticola / R. solani\): Sudden wilting in patches; shredded bark on roots. Manage by intercropping with Mothbean/Sorghum.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 401 Td (- Grey Mildew \(Ramularia areola\) & Alternaria Leaf Spot: Frosty white growth on lower leaves or concentric brown rings. Spray Azoxystrobin + Tebuconazole.) Tj ET

BT /F2 10 Tf 35 381 Td (9. Defoliation, Harvesting, Post-Harvest & Fiber Quality Grading) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 368 Td (- Defoliation & Boll Opening: For mechanical picking, apply Thidiazuron + Diuron \(at 60% boll opening\) and Ethephon 39 SL to synchronize boll opening.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 356 Td (- Harvesting Protocol: Pick dry seed-cotton \(Kapas\) in morning hours after dew evaporates; keep 3-4 pickings separate \(first & last pickings are inferior\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 344 Td (- Post-Harvest Storage: Dry Kapas in shade to <8-10% moisture; store in clean cotton cloth bags \(avoid polypropylene bags to prevent fiber contamination\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 332 Td (- Ginning & Parameters: Ginning Outturn \(GOT\) is typically 32-36% lint and 64-68% seed. High Volume Instrument \(HVI\) grades: Upper Half Mean Length) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 35 320 Td (  \(UHML: Short <20 mm, Long 25-30 mm, Extra-Long >32 mm\), Micronaire \(fineness: optimal 3.5-4.9\), Bundle Tenacity \(>28 g/tex\), and Trash Content.) Tj ET
endstream
